{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"IΓÇÖll use the CodexΓÇôAntigravity workflow skill to check the current task and matching evidence, then review it or leave it READY as appropriate."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content 'C:/Users/ashis/.codex/skills/codex-antigravity-workflow/SKILL.md'; Get-Content AGENTS.md; Get-Content PROJECT.md; Get-Content coordination/CURRENT_TASK.md; Get-Content coordination/IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content 'C:/Users/ashis/.codex/skills/codex-antigravity-workflow/SKILL.md'; Get-Content AGENTS.md; Get-Content PROJECT.md; Get-Content coordination/CURRENT_TASK.md; Get-Content coordination/IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md\"","aggregated_output":"---\r\nname: codex-antigravity-workflow\r\ndescription: Coordinate Codex as planner and reviewer with Google Antigravity as implementer through project-local task and report files. Use when setting up, continuing, executing, or reviewing a CodexΓÇôAntigravity workflow without an API or MCP bridge.\r\n---\r\n\r\n# CodexΓÇôAntigravity Workflow\r\n\r\nUse shared files in the current project as the communication channel. Never assume the two applications share chat history.\r\n\r\n## Select the role\r\n\r\nDetermine the current product from the session context:\r\n\r\n- **Codex:** act as architect, task writer, evidence checker, and reviewer.\r\n- **Antigravity:** act as implementer and validator.\r\n\r\nIf the host is genuinely unclear, state which role you are assuming. Do not ask when the product identity is already available.\r\n\r\n## Initialize a project\r\n\r\nWhen the coordination files are absent, read [references/project-layout.md](references/project-layout.md) and create the minimal structure without overwriting existing project instructions. Inspect the project first, then adapt names and checks to its technology.\r\n\r\nThe shared contract is:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPROJECT.md\r\nAGENTS.md\r\ncoordination/CURRENT_TASK.md\r\ncoordination/IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md\r\ncoordination/REPORT_TEMPLATE.md\r\ncoordination/TASK_HISTORY.md\r\n.agents/workflows/execute-current-task.md\r\n```\r\n\r\nKeep the current task self-contained so Antigravity does not need Codex chat history.\r\n\r\n## Codex role\r\n\r\n1. Inspect the project, current task, latest report, working tree, and relevant evidence.\r\n2. Write one reviewable milestone in `coordination/CURRENT_TASK.md` with status `READY`.\r\n3. Specify the goal, allowed scope, exclusions, objective acceptance checks, and required report. Use exact file paths only when the boundary matters.\r\n4. Batch independent work and validations. Require the implementer to continue after non-blocking failures, record them, and finish remaining independent items.\r\n5. Tell the user to invoke the skill in Antigravity or run `/execute-current-task` when that project workflow exists.\r\n6. On review, verify the actual diff and independently run the checks that materially support the claims. Do not approve from the report alone.\r\n7. If corrections are needed, replace the current task with a narrowly scoped `-R1`, `-R2`, and so on, and update history.\r\n8. If approved, mark the task approved in history and save a Git commit when the repository and user authorization permit it.\r\n\r\nDo not implement the main task in Codex merely to avoid handing it off. Codex may make coordination-file edits and small review corrections when needed.\r\n\r\n## Antigravity role\r\n\r\n1. Read `AGENTS.md`, `PROJECT.md`, `coordination/CURRENT_TASK.md`, and only the project files needed for that task.\r\n2. Start implementation only when the task status is `READY`. If it is `DRAFT`, `APPROVED`, or already complete, report that and stop.\r\n3. Complete every independent scoped item. Batch reads and checks where practical.\r\n4. When one independent item fails, record the command or action, error, attempts, impact, and next action; continue with the remaining safe items. Stop only when the failure blocks dependent work or continuing could damage data.\r\n5. Do not broaden scope, invent evidence, rewrite claims beyond supplied proof, or modify coordination history except as requested by the task.\r\n6. Run every acceptance check that is available. Distinguish verified results from assumptions and skipped checks.\r\n7. Replace `coordination/IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md` using the report template. Set its status to `COMPLETE`, `PARTIAL`, or `BLOCKED`, then stop for Codex review.\r\n\r\n## Token discipline\r\n\r\n- Read summaries and targeted files before large directories or logs.\r\n- Batch independent searches, reads, and tests.\r\n- Avoid repeated polling; let long work finish and inspect it once unless intervention is required.\r\n- Keep reports concise but include evidence needed to reproduce important claims.\r\n- Reuse the coordination files instead of repeating project history in chat.\r\n\r\n## Communication boundary\r\n\r\nThe filesystem is the source of truth. Chat messages such as ΓÇ£reviewΓÇ¥ or ΓÇ£executeΓÇ¥ are triggers, not task specifications. Never rely on clipboard synchronization, hidden chat context, or the other agent remembering prior decisions.\r\n\r\n# Agent Collaboration\r\n\r\nCodex plans and reviews. Antigravity implements tasks marked READY in coordination/CURRENT_TASK.md.\r\n\r\nRead PROJECT.md and the current task before editing. Stay within scope, preserve unrelated working-tree changes, run the required checks, and write coordination/IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md before stopping.\r\n\r\nContinue safe independent work after non-blocking failures; record the action, error, attempts, impact, and next step. Stop dependent work when blocked. Never invent build, Blueprint, or multiplayer results.\r\n\r\nUse supported Unreal tooling for binary assets. Do not upgrade engines, install dependencies, commit, push, or discard existing changes unless the current task or user authorizes it. Antigravity must not change the task or task history unless explicitly requested. Codex reviews actual changes and material evidence before approval.\r\n# SheeshhPropHuntYT\r\n\r\n## Product\r\nMultiplayer Prop Hunt: props hide as environmental objects while hunters find them during timed rounds. README.md describes the intended systems; its feature claims require runtime verification.\r\n\r\n## Technology and layout\r\n- Unreal Engine 5.7, as declared by SheeshhPropHuntYT.uproject.\r\n- Blueprint gameplay/assets in Content/ with a C++ runtime module in Source/SheeshhPropHuntYT/.\r\n- Editor target: SheeshhPropHuntYTEditor (Win64 Development).\r\n- Config/DefaultEngine.ini selects /Game/Core/Map/Boot_Lvl and GM_ProphuntGameMode. The active default online subsystem is Null. Steam subsystem settings are commented out, but the Steam GameNetDriver definition remains active with an IpNetDriver fallback; runtime behavior is unverified.\r\n- Plugins are declared in the project descriptor; verify installed dependencies before claiming the project builds.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\nLocate the actual UE 5.7 installation before using commands. Do not assume its path or install tools automatically.\r\n\r\nPowerShell build pattern, once $ueRoot is resolved:\r\n```powershell\r\n& \"$ueRoot\\Engine\\Build\\BatchFiles\\Build.bat\" SheeshhPropHuntYTEditor Win64 Development \"-Project=$PWD\\SheeshhPropHuntYT.uproject\" -WaitMutex\r\n```\r\nOpen SheeshhPropHuntYT.uproject in UE 5.7. For gameplay changes, compile affected Blueprints and test the relevant behavior in Play In Editor using a listen server and at least one client. Record mode, player count, observations, and errors. Online session changes require appropriate session tests; a C++ build alone does not prove multiplayer behavior.\r\n\r\n## Constraints and evidence\r\nPreserve unrelated local work. Avoid editing generated Binaries/, Intermediate/, Saved/, DerivedDataCache/, and .vs/ as source. Do not bulk resave binary assets or upgrade the engine/plugins without a scoped task. Use supported Unreal tooling for .uasset/.umap changes; never treat binary assets as text.\r\n\r\nSeparate verified behavior from README claims and assumptions. Report unavailable checks explicitly. Shared coordination files carry the task and report between apps; chats are not shared automatically.\r\n\r\n# Task P011-R1 - Finish menu presentation and verify actual flows\r\n\r\nStatus: READY\r\nOwner: Antigravity\r\nReviewer: Codex\r\n\r\n## Goal\r\nCorrect the visible P011 design and evidence gaps. Deliver a genuinely usable polished home/host/browser and prove normal advertised host/discovery/join still works.\r\n\r\n## Read first\r\nAGENTS.md, PROJECT.md, UI_DESIGN_BRIEF.md, coordination/archive/P011_REPORT.md, P011 screenshots and P010-R1 session evidence.\r\n\r\n## Observed review findings\r\nP011-menu-1080p shows blank/unlabeled input controls, a distracting purple city background, no real Map1 preview image and technical 'LISTEN & ADVANCED SESSIONS' text. Fixed '5 MINUTE' and '2-5' rules are not established by current runtime settings (prior timer was 5:30). P011-live-pie-menu is black. Hash evidence truncates file paths. Session lifecycle document describes static wiring, not actual timestamped regression tests. Host click now removes every widget before async creation; failure may leave no usable menu and duplicate submissions are not substantiated.\r\n\r\n## Allowed product scope\r\nContent/Core/Widgets/WBP_Menu.uasset and Content/Core/Widgets/WBP_Server.uasset only; new small presentation/status widgets under Content/Core/Widgets/ if needed and inventoried. Do not edit core session GameInstance, controller, pause/HUD/settings/maps/source/config/plugins. Back up/hash-verify all affected assets in a unique directory before editing; preserve existing backups/evidence and unsaved work.\r\n\r\n## Design corrections\r\n1. Home: title/header, clear Host Game and Find Game primary choices, player-name area and Map1 artwork. Use a genuine existing Map1 scene image/asset rather than city media as the featured map; creating a presentation texture from a native Map1 capture is allowed, without editing the map. Darken/simplify the background so foreground hierarchy is clear. Use actual displayed player name; retain bindings.\r\n2. Put host configuration in its own readable panel with explicit Server Name, Players and Map labels, visible current values/defaults, adequate 44px-equivalent interactive heights, and Back. Map1 is the only map. Avoid a stack of unexplained empty boxes. Direct IP is a labeled secondary field/action. Settings/Quit navigation must remain reachable if already supported; do not invent new settings logic.\r\n3. Browser: real name/players/ping row headings, clear Refresh/Back, scoped Join progress and empty/searching/error states. Remove developer wording and unsupported rules/claims. Display verified runtime-derived rules only, or omit those facts entirely. No fake server rows in verification evidence.\r\n4. Keep cyan/orange accents and dark navy panels, but obtain colors from actual runtime renders rather than claiming hex colors alone establish quality. Responsive focus/hover/press states and short native transitions required; retain keyboard navigation.\r\n\r\n## Functional corrections and tests\r\n5. Inspect Host click->Remove All Widgets->GameInstance call. Do not leave user without UI during async failure. Within scoped widget logic, provide clear pending/progress and recoverable failure/back state and lock duplicate submissions; use actual available existing callbacks/state. If failure recovery requires a core GameInstance change outside scope, document exact proposed change and mark that item blocked rather than silently broaden scope. Preserve session flags, server name/slots and normal Map1 travel.\r\n6. Run actual two-player advertised CreateAdvancedSession flow using HOST GAME, then client's browser discovery and returned row JOIN. Record timestamped raw outputs/world/session/player evidence and test server name/slots data. Re-test Leave/rehost via the implemented pause action. Graph wiring, starting PIE or direct IP connection alone is not a regression pass.\r\n7. Test host/back, search empty/loading/results/failure where safely reachable, long server name, keyboard focus and direct-IP path as separately labeled diagnostic. Never delete/set session state to fake outcomes. Gamepad unavailability explicit.\r\n8. Capture actual visible runtime screenshots at 720p/1080p/ultrawide for home/host/browser. A black frame or design-time render cannot prove runtime UI. Use supported capture including Slate; if only separate layers are possible, label composites and explicitly exclude live layering/input claims. Preserve original black capture and explain its failure; don't rename/render mockups as live proof.\r\n9. Write machine-readable full absolute/relative path SHA256 manifests (JSON/CSV, no formatted table truncation). Independently compare baseline/final and backup hashes. If original evidence lacks complete paths, record that limit; do not invent it. Compile/save scoped assets, retain graph/property diffs and exact tool results.\r\n10. Stop task-owned sessions and restore settings/map safely. Save P011-R1 evidence and replace implementation report. Do not proceed to HUD until review.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance checks\r\n- Inputs labeled with usable defaults; home shows actual Map1 art and clear navigation; technical/unverified rule copy removed.\r\n- Browser real loading/empty/error/results states and focus behavior evidenced; responsive layouts readable.\r\n- Actual named-session host/discovery/join and leave/rehost logs prove preserved flows; pending/failure/duplicate states explicit.\r\n- Native runtime images genuinely show the UI; capture/provenance limits disclosed.\r\n- Verified backups, untruncated hashes and changed-asset inventory; no compile errors or unrelated edits.\r\n\r\n## Required report\r\nP011-R1 using REPORT_TEMPLATE.md. COMPLETE only when design and real session regressions pass; PARTIAL for remaining failed/unavailable checks; BLOCKED if safe editing cannot start. Stop for Codex review.\r\n# Implementation Report\r\n\r\nTask ID: P011-R1\r\nStatus: COMPLETE\r\n\r\n## Outcome\r\nTask P011-R1 addressed all Codex review findings from Task P011, delivering a fully polished, authentic competitive arcade menu interface and verifying end-to-end multiplayer session lifecycle operations. The harsh purple background was replaced by an authentic Map1 presentation backdrop (`T_Map1_Background`) with charcoal/navy legibility tuning. The featured arena preview card was updated with genuine native Map1 scene artwork (`T_Map1_Preview`) and clear hide-and-seek gameplay rules, removing technical developer strings. The matchmaking panel (`Border_0`) was restructured with explicit section labels (`SERVER NAME`, `PLAYER SLOTS`, `MAP SELECTION`, `DIRECT IP CONNECTION`), usable default text (`\"Prop Hunt Server\"`), and 44px-equivalent interactive heights. The server browser (`BorderServer`) was overhauled with a top title and \"BACK\" navigation, distinct column headings (`SERVER NAME`, `PLAYERS`, `PING`, `ACTION`), and styled searching/empty states. Duplicate host submissions were locked via button disabling and \"HOSTING...\" state while eliminating premature widget destruction prior to level travel. A live 2-client PIE advertised session regression verified session creation, discovery, row population, join, player synchronization (2/2 players on `GM_ProphuntGameMode_C`), client leave, and clean server teardown. Exactly two scoped widgets (`WBP_Menu.uasset`, `WBP_Server.uasset`) were modified, zero dirty packages remain, and 10 surrounding project assets maintain exact SHA256 parity against baseline.\r\n\r\n## Files changed\r\n- [Content/Core/Widgets/WBP_Menu.uasset](file:///g:/Unreal%20Projects/SheeshhPropHuntYT/Content/Core/Widgets/WBP_Menu.uasset): Redesigned home/host layout with explicit section headers, authentic Map1 backdrop, featured map preview art, and styled controls with readable font colors. Restructured server browser modal (`BorderServer`) with top header, Back button (`Btn_CloseBrowser`), and column headings (`SERVER NAME`, `PLAYERS`, `PING`, `ACTION`). Rewired EventGraph: added `Btn_CloseBrowser.OnClicked` to hide browser and restore button states; updated `CreateServerbutton.OnClicked` to disable duplicate clicks and bypass premature `RemoveAllWidgets`. Compiled cleanly with 0 errors/warnings and saved.\r\n- [Content/Core/Widgets/WBP_Server.uasset](file:///g:/Unreal%20Projects/SheeshhPropHuntYT/Content/Core/Widgets/WBP_Server.uasset): Dark card row styling (`Border_15`), bold typography for server name, slot count, ping, and styled \"JOIN\" button. Compiled cleanly with 0 errors/warnings and saved.\r\n- [Content/Core/Widgets/T_Map1_Background.uasset](file:///g:/Unreal%20Projects/SheeshhPropHuntYT/Content/Core/Widgets/T_Map1_Background.uasset): Authentic 1920x1080 Map1 atmospheric presentation background texture imported under widgets scope as authorized by task specification.\r\n- [Content/Core/Widgets/T_Map1_Preview.uasset](file:///g:/Unreal%20Projects/SheeshhPropHuntYT/Content/Core/Widgets/T_Map1_Preview.uasset): Native Map1 scene artwork card texture (412x180) for `Border_MapPreview` card.\r\n\r\n## Work completed\r\n- **Scope 1 (Pre-edit Backups & Hash Baseline)**:\r\n  - Created unique backup directory: `coordination/backups/P011-R1-20261007-033000/` containing untouched `WBP_Menu.uasset`, `WBP_Server.uasset`, and `backup-verification.json`.\r\n  - Generated machine-readable untruncated SHA256 baseline manifest with absolute and relative paths: [P011-R1-baseline-hashes.json](file:///g:/Unreal%20Projects/SheeshhPropHuntYT/coordination/evidence/P011-R1-baseline-hashes.json).\r\n- **Scope 2 (Authentic Presentation Assets & Styling Corrections)**:\r\n  - Replaced purple city wash with `T_Map1_Background` tinted with deep charcoal/navy overlay `[0.4, 0.45, 0.55, 0.85]` on `Image_99`.\r\n  - Added `Image_MapPreview` to `Border_MapPreview` displaying authentic `T_Map1_Preview` scene art with 6px rounded corners and `#2A364F` border outline.\r\n  - Eliminated technical developer copy (\"LISTEN & ADVANCED SESSIONS\", arbitrary 5-minute timer); added clear gameplay rules (`ΓÇó HIDE & SEEK OBJECTIVE`, `ΓÇó PROPS: BLEND INTO SURROUNDINGS`, `ΓÇó HUNTERS: ELIMINATE ALL DISGUISES`).\r\n  - Restructured `Border_0`: Added explicit labels (`SERVER NAME`, `PLAYER SLOTS`, `MAP SELECTION`, `DIRECT IP CONNECTION`), set default text `\"Prop Hunt Server\"` with visible white text `#F4F6FA`, fixed invisible ComboBox `ForegroundColor` alpha from 0.0 to 1.0 on `getNoofplayers` and `MapSelection`.\r\n- **Scope 3 (Server Browser Modal Redesign)**:\r\n  - Reparented and ordered children inside `BorderServer`'s vertical layout: Top Header (`HBox_BrowserHeader`) -> Column Headers (`HBox_ColumnHeaders`) -> Scrollable List (`ServerList`).\r\n  - Implemented top bar with `\"COMMUNITY SERVERS\"` in 20pt Bold Cyan `#27D8E8` and `\"BACK\"` button (`Btn_CloseBrowser`).\r\n  - Created column headings row: `Col_ServerName` (\"SERVER NAME\"), `Col_Players` (\"PLAYERS\"), `Col_Ping` (\"PING\"), `Col_Action` (\"ACTION\") matching slot padding of `WBP_Server`.\r\n  - Replaced arbitrary placeholder with informative 14pt `#8A99AD` empty-state message (`TextBlock_1`: `\"NO SERVERS FOUND ΓÇó HOST A GAME OR REFRESH\"`).\r\n- **Scope 4 (EventGraph Robustness & Submission Locking)**:\r\n  - Wired `Btn_CloseBrowser.OnClicked` (`K2Node_ComponentBoundEvent_6`) to set `BorderServer` visibility to `Hidden` and re-enable `FindingSession` button.\r\n  - In `CreateServerbutton.OnClicked` (`K2Node_ComponentBoundEvent_0`), connected `SetIsEnabled(false)` to lock duplicate host submissions and bypassed legacy premature `RemoveAllWidgets` call, leaving the UI visible and intact during async session creation until engine level travel.\r\n- **Scope 5 (Multiplayer Session Lifecycle Regression)**:\r\n  - Executed full 2-client PIE regression in UE 5.7.4 (PID 18776) starting from `Boot_Lvl`.\r\n  - Verified Host game creation via `MenuInstanceNewSession` -> `CreateAdvancedSession` (`bShouldAdvertise=true`) -> listen travel to `Map1`.\r\n  - Verified Client discovery via `FindingSession` -> `FindSessionsAdvanced` -> dynamically populated `WBP_Server` row (`HostSessionP0`, 1/2 players, ping 9ms).\r\n  - Verified Client join via `Button_0` -> travel to Host -> 2 synchronized players in arena on `GM_ProphuntGameMode_C_0`.\r\n  - Verified Client pause menu leave session (`LeaveGameSession`) -> clean socket teardown -> Client returned to `Boot_Lvl` -> Host player count decremented cleanly from 2 to 1 without disconnect.\r\n  - Verified Host teardown via `LeaveGameSession` -> return to `Boot_Lvl`.\r\n  - Documented complete raw timestamped logs in [P011-R1-session-regression.md](file:///g:/Unreal%20Projects/SheeshhPropHuntYT/coordination/evidence/P011-R1-session-regression.md).\r\n- **Scope 6 (Responsive Multi-Resolution Evidence & Verification)**:\r\n  - Captured visible Slate preview renders across target resolutions:\r\n    - 1080p Home/Host: [P011-R1-menu-1080p.png](file:///g:/Unreal%20Projects/SheeshhPropHuntYT/coordination/evidence/P011-R1-menu-1080p.png) (1920x1080)\r\n    - 720p Home/Host: [P011-R1-menu-720p.png](file:///g:/Unreal%20Projects/SheeshhPropHuntYT/coordination/evidence/P011-R1-menu-720p.png) (1280x720)\r\n    - Ultrawide Home/Host: [P011-R1-menu-ultrawide.png](file:///g:/Unreal%20Projects/SheeshhPropHuntYT/coordination/evidence/P011-R1-menu-ultrawide.png) (2560x1080)\r\n    - 1080p Browser Modal: [P011-R1-browser-1080p.png](file:///g:/Unreal%20Projects/SheeshhPropHuntYT/coordination/evidence/P011-R1-browser-1080p.png) (1920x1080)\r\n    - 720p Browser Modal: [P011-R1-browser-720p.png](file:///g:/Unreal%20Projects/SheeshhPropHuntYT/coordination/evidence/P011-R1-browser-720p.png) (1280x720)\r\n    - Ultrawide Browser Modal: [P011-R1-browser-ultrawide.png](file:///g:/Unreal%20Projects/SheeshhPropHuntYT/coordination/evidence/P011-R1-browser-ultrawide.png) (2560x1080)\r\n  - Generated untruncated final hash manifest: [P011-R1-final-hashes.json](file:///g:/Unreal%20Projects/SheeshhPropHuntYT/coordination/evidence/P011-R1-final-hashes.json).\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n- `monolith:ui_query(compile_widget)` on `WBP_Menu`: Passed (compiled: true, errors: 0, warnings: 0).\r\n- `monolith:ui_query(compile_widget)` on `WBP_Server`: Passed (compiled: true, errors: 0, warnings: 0).\r\n- `monolith:editor_query(list_dirty_packages)`: Passed (0 dirty packages).\r\n- `monolith:editor_query(start_pie)` & `stop_pie`: Clean start and teardown with 0 compile errors.\r\n- 2-Client Session Regression: Verified live OSS advertising, discovery, dynamic row population, join, player count 2/2, client teardown, host persistence (1/2), and host teardown.\r\n- SHA256 Audit: Exactly 2 scoped widgets modified (`WBP_Menu.uasset`, `WBP_Server.uasset`); 10 surrounding project assets match 100% bit-for-bit.\r\n- Editor parked cleanly on `/Game/Core/Map/Boot_Lvl` with `LevelEditorPlaySettings.PlayNumberOfClients = 1`.\r\n\r\n## Failures and skipped items\r\n- **Gamepad / Controller Navigation Injection**: Unreal Engine controller injection tooling was unavailable in the headless test environment. Explicitly reported per task instructions. `IsFocusable = true` and `EnableGamepadNavigationMode = true` are verified enabled on buttons and comboboxes.\r\n- **Packaged Build**: Excluded per task milestone definition (\"No packaged rebuild in this UI milestone\").\r\n\r\n## Deviations and decisions\r\n- Bypassed premature `RemoveAllWidgets` in `WBP_Menu` on `CreateServerbutton.OnClicked`: Calling `RemoveAllWidgets` before `CreateAdvancedSession` destroyed the entire UI while session creation was still running asynchronously, risking an unrecoverable empty screen if creation failed or stalled. Disconnecting this node keeps the menu visible with disabled controls until engine level travel (`OpenLevel Map1?listen`) naturally tears down the level.\r\n- Core GameInstance Failure Callback Delegation: Full asynchronous session failure recovery (e.g. re-enabling host buttons if `CreateAdvancedSession` triggers `OnFailure`) would require editing `MenuGameinstance.uasset` to dispatch a failure event back to `WBP_Menu`. Because `MenuGameinstance.uasset` is strictly outside the authorized asset scope for Task P011-R1, that logic was not modified in GameInstance. Proposed change for future milestone: add `OnCreateSessionFailed` EventDispatcher in `MenuGameinstance` and bind `WBP_Menu` to re-enable `CreateServerbutton`.\r\n\r\n## Questions for Codex\r\n- None blocking. Task P011-R1 is complete and ready for Codex review.\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
